{title: 206 - Face to Face}
{subtitle: SDA Hymnal #206 • }
{lyricist: }
{composer: }
{key: Bb}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: Moderato}
{meta: hymn_number 206}
{meta: category Jesus Christ - }

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[Bb]Face to face with Christ my [Cm7]Sav[F7]iour, Face to face, what will it [Bb]be,
[Bb]When with rapture I [Eb]behold Him, [Edim7]Jesus [Bb]Christ, who [Dm]died [F7]for [Bb]me?
[F7]Face to face shall [Bb]I behold Him, [F]Far be[C7]yond the starry [F]sk[Bb]y;[F7]
[Bb]Face to face in all His [Eb]glory [Edim7]I shall [Bb]see Him [Dm]by [F7]and [Bb]by!
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Refrain}
[Bb]Face [Cm7]to face [F7]shall I [Bb]behold Him,
[Bb][Eb]Far [Edim7]beyond [Bb][Dm]the [F7]starry [Bb]sky;
[F7]Face [Bb]to [F]face [C7]in [F]all [Bb]His [F7]glory
[Bb]I [Eb]shall [Edim7]see [Bb]Him [Dm]by [F7]and [Bb]by!
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[Bb]Only [Cm7]faintly now [F7]I [Bb]see Him,
[Bb][Eb]With [Edim7]the [Bb][Dm]darkening [F7]veil [Bb]between,
[F7][Bb]But [F]a [C7]blessed [F]day [Bb]is [F7]coming,
[Bb][Eb]When [Edim7]His [Bb]glory [Dm]shall [F7]be [Bb]seen.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[Bb]What [Cm7]rejoicing [F7]in [Bb]His presence,
[Bb][Eb]When [Edim7]are [Bb]banished [Dm]grief [F7]and [Bb]pain;
[F7][Bb]When [F]the [C7]crooked [F]ways [Bb]are [F7]straightened,
[Bb]And [Eb]the [Edim7]dark [Bb]things [Dm]shall [F7]be [Bb]plain!
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 4}
[Bb]Face [Cm7]to face! [F7]oh, [Bb]blissful moment!
[Bb]Face [Eb]to [Edim7]face [Bb]to [Dm]see [F7]and [Bb]know;
[F7][Bb]Face [F]to [C7]face [F]with [Bb]my [F7]Redeemer,
[Bb][Eb]Jesus [Edim7]Christ, [Bb]who [Dm]loves [F7]me [Bb]so.
{end_of_verse}
